# Title: Suspicious Velociraptor Child Process
# ID: 4bc90587-e6ca-4b41-be0b-ed4d04e4ed0c
# Status: experimental
# Level: high
# Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2025-08-29
# Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.persistence, attack.t1219
# Description: Detects the suspicious use of the Velociraptor DFIR tool to execute other tools or download additional payloads, as seen in a campaign where it was abused for remote access and to stage further attacks.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog ((parent_process_path="*\\Velociraptor.exe") AND (((process_exec="*msiexec*" AND process_exec="*/i*" AND process_exec="*http*")) OR ((process_path="*\\powershell.exe" OR process_path="*\\powershell_ise.exe" OR process_path="*\\pwsh.exe") AND (process_exec="*Invoke-WebRequest *" OR process_exec="*IWR *" OR process_exec="*.DownloadFile*" OR process_exec="*.DownloadString*")) OR ((process_exec="*code.exe*" AND process_exec="*tunnel*" AND process_exec="*--accept-server-license-terms*"))))
